cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "positscale: optimal diagonal scaling for posit arithmetic"
abstract: >-
  Posit precision is tapered, peaking at unit magnitude, so operand placement
  is a numerical design variable in a way it is not for IEEE 754. This software
  formulates posit-optimal diagonal scaling as a convex programme, solves it
  exactly, and shows the optimum coincides with the maximum mean cycle weight
  of a bipartite log-magnitude digraph.
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-08-17
license: MIT
